On Sunday 13 June 2010 05:24:29 lojdjis wrote:
> I would like to know what will be names for chemicla elements like
> Radium, Palladium.

zo dircyjinme .e zo jinmrpaladi

> M.b. it's better to invent new words something like
>
> "xukmi'a'u" or "la a'us." or "xu'i'a'u" for Au (Aurum)
> "xukmi'fu'e" or "la fu'es." or "xu'ifu'e" for Fe (Ferrum)
> "xukmixe'e" or "la xe'es." or "xu'ixe'e" for He (Helium)
> "xukminu'i" or "la nu'is." or "xu'inu'i" for Ni (Nickel).

First, as three of those have gismu, that's unnecessary. (The other one is 
solnavni.) Second, the first word in each set is the wrong kind of fu'ivla 
(except "xukmi'fu'e" which isn't a word at all), and the third is a cmavo or 
string of cmavo.

http://jbo.wikipedia.org/wiki/dikni_selratni_cartu (should be "dikni selratni 
bo cartu", as it is, it's "table of periodic elements"). "sodna" should 
be "xasysodna" or some such; "sodna" by itself refers to the whole column. 
Similarly for "kliru".

